<title>UK: GECC adds $100 million to four-year bond.</title>
<headline>GECC adds $100 million to four-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been increased to $350 million from $250 million, lead manager SBC Warburg said.</p>
<p> BORROWER   GENERAL ELECTRIC CAPITAL CORP </p>
<p> AMT   *$350 MLN	COUPON     6.25	MATURITY    13.FEB.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE**102.045   PAY DATE    13.FEB.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.625     SPREAD     6 BP	PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> NOTES     *LAUNCHED ORIGINALLY FOR $250 MLN ON 13.JAN.97</p>
<p>	    **NEW ISSUE PRICE.</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AAA/AAA   DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.225     SELL CONC  1.40	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF AN EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
